    <decisions>
        <description>On successful debtor delete the BillectaId__c is set to null on Account. We only want to delete Account after the Debtor has been deleted in Billecta first. 
1. day, the  Account debtor in Billecta is deleted using the apex action. 
2. day, account runs in this flow again and now BillectaId is null - hence attempting to delete the account.</description>
        <name>BillectaId_c_is_populated</name>
        <label>BillectaId__c is populated?</label>
        <locationX>182</locationX>
        <locationY>1058</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Pause_to_start_new_transaction</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No (null)</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Yes_billectaIdNotNull</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_current_Account.BillectaID__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Delete_Billecta_Debtor</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Yes</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
